# terminfo source for puppy, a from-scratch Python terminal emulator targeting
# kitty-protocol parity (https://github.com/pamperedgenius/puppy).
#
# Deliberately inherits from xterm-256color (`use=`) rather than being written
# fully from scratch. This is honest, not lazy: input-side capabilities (k* key
# sequences) genuinely ARE xterm's right now, since puppy's PTY proxy is a pure
# pass-through on the input side (see __main__.py) -- whatever the *host* terminal
# actually sends when a key is pressed reaches the child unmodified, because
# puppy doesn't yet intercept/regenerate key events itself (that's blocked on the
# windowing-toolkit decision, see PROGRESS.md). Output-side capabilities that
# puppy's Parser/Screen genuinely implement are inherited as-is when xterm-256color
# already states them correctly (e.g. bce, ccc, initc -- all confirmed real via
# source-level verification, see PROGRESS.md, not just assumed compatible) and only
# overridden below where puppy's actual behavior differs from xterm's. Anything
# neither implemented nor overridden is simply inherited and, per the parser's own
# "not yet implemented, silently ignored" pattern, harmless if a program sends it:
# puppy won't crash, it just won't act on it yet.
#
# Overrides below:
# - rmcup/smcup: trimmed to exactly mode 1049 (cursor save/restore included, see
#   PROGRESS.md's kitty-source verification pass) -- the xterm-inherited
#   window-title-stack tail bytes (23/22;0;0t) aren't implemented by the parser
#   (unhandled CSI ...t is silently ignored, harmless but pointless to advertise).
# - Tc, RGB: 24-bit truecolor SGR (38/48;2;r;g;b, both ';' and ':' sub-parameter
#   forms including the colorspace-id variant) -- Screen.sgr supports this fully,
#   xterm-256color itself doesn't advertise it. Both extension-capability names are
#   declared since different tools check different ones (tmux historically checks
#   Tc, ncurses/newer tools check RGB) -- see terminfo.dev's truecolor-detection
#   convention.
#
# Update this file's overrides whenever a milestone lands new Screen/Parser
# capability that diverges from xterm-256color -- don't let it silently drift.

puppy|puppy-256color|puppy terminal emulator (kitty-protocol parity WIP),
	use=xterm-256color,
	rmcup=\E[?1049l, smcup=\E[?1049h,
	Tc, RGB,
